's flatwater windsurf mecca, beginner-friendly and world-class, in a RAMSAR wetland","when":"year-round; windiest May-Jul","commission":"operator/affiliate 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","ocean":"primary","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Washington Slagbaai National Park","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-60 + $40 nature fee","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the rugged northwest — a 4,286-ha park, 4×4 tracks, cliffs, blowholes, salt pans and inland flamingo lakes","si":"adventure","blurb":"the rugged northwest — a 4,286-ha park, 4×4 tracks, cliffs, blowholes, salt pans and inland flamingo lakes","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"operator/affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Flamingos + the sea-turtle nesting shores","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-70/pp","timing":"year-round; turtles seasonal","draw_rank":1,"hook":"RAMSAR wetlands with resident flamingos, and beaches that nest all four Caribbean sea-turtle species — a genuine wildlife layer beside the reef","si":"adventure","blurb":"RAMSAR wetlands with resident flamingos, and beaches that nest all four Caribbean sea-turtle species — a genuine wildlife layer beside the reef","when":"year-round; turtles seasonal","commission":"operator/affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["adventure","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bonaire?","a":"Dive discipline, not danger. Because Bonaire is 24/7 drive-up shore diving, hold the no-fly 18-24h window and manage repetitive profiles. The on-island hyperbaric chamber next to the Kralendijk hospital is 24-hour and operational (2026).","source":"o2bonaire.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I have to pay the Bonaire nature fee and what does it cost?","a":"Yes - a mandatory US$40 STINAPA nature tag for all water activities (2026); it funds no-touch/no-anchor enforcement, fish surveys and reef restoration, and also covers Washington Slagbaai NP. Buy it online before you dive.","source":"bonaire.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Bonaire?","a":"Year-round, but December-April is peak (cooler water, best visibility) and April-August brings the calmest seas and superb viz - Bonaire is south of the hurricane belt so there''s no real storm season.","source":"habitatbonaire.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Which Bonaire dive sites should I not miss?","a":"The Hilma Hooker wreck (30m), 1000 Steps (shallow, snorkel-friendly), Salt Pier (pillar ecosystems - only when no ship is in port) and a Klein Bonaire boat day; most of the ~89 sites are self-guided drive-and-dive off the yellow stones.","source":"scubatravel.co.uk","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Bonaire a liveaboard destination?","a":"No - Bonaire is the world''s shore/drive-and-dive capital (unlimited-shore packages, drive-thru tank pickup), not a liveaboard base. Book it as a resort-and-shore dive trip, not a Dive Liveaboards sailing.","source":"zubludiving.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bonaire Travel Guide: The Shore-Diving Capital, Marine Park & Nature Fee","meta_description":"Plan Bonaire - the shore-diving capital of the world: ~89 marked marine-park sites you drive up and walk into, the Hilma Hooker wreck, the $40 STINAPA nature fee, an on-island recompression chamber, flamingos and Lac Bay windsurf.","slug":"bonaire","primary_keyword":"Bonaire shore diving","long_tail":["Bonaire shore diving guide 2026","Bonaire National Marine Park dive sites","Hilma Hooker wreck dive","Bonaire STINAPA nature fee","Klein Bonaire boat dive","Lac Bay windsurfing"],"search_language":"nl","local_keywords":["Boneiru","Marine Park Boneiru","Hilma Hooker","STINAPA nature fee","Klein Bonaire","Lac Bay windsurf","Washington Slagbaai"],"hreflang":["en","nl"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-30","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-30","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bonaire-st-eustatius-saba","read":"2026-08-19","source_updated":"2025-12-10T13:10:48+00:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":[],"note":"Dutch green code; south of the hurricane belt; USD currency"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-30","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; Dive Liveaboards is a hard MISS (shore/day-boat, NOT liveaboard); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status